  "title": "Rebound Bro",
  "cn": "第 18 集 · 替补兄弟",
  "novel": "Ted [[found|find]] a [[rebound|rebound]] best friend named Randy. Barney [[attempted|attempt]] to find his own replacement, but every [[candidate|candidate]] [[failed|fail]].\n\nRandy was [[awkward|awkward]] and [[eager|eager]] to please. He [[laughed|laugh]] at Ted's jokes, even the bad ones. \"You're my new best friend,\" Ted [[declared|declare]].\n\nBut the [[friendship|friendship]] felt [[forced|force]]. Randy tried too hard. He [[agreed|agree]] with everything Ted said. There was no [[spark|spark]], no [[connection|connection]].\n\nBarney, meanwhile, [[found|find]] a man named Joe. Joe was [[perfect|perfect]] — until he fell into a [[coma|coma]]. \"My rebound bro is in a coma,\" Barney [[complained|complain]].\n\nTed [[realized|realize]] that friendships, like [[romance|romance]], couldn't be [[forced|force]]. They [[happened|happen]] naturally or not at all.\n\nHe thanked Randy and let him go. Some replacements, Ted learned, only reminded you of what you'd lost.",
